=== SURVEY ===
Baseline (non-AI) surface kept canonical (ADR-015 §I3):
  - Frontend page: web/src/features/notifications/pages/QuietHoursPage.tsx
    Wraps QuietHoursPanel inside PageContainer; deterministic CRUD list,
    "Add window" button, per-row Edit/Delete, canonical Save button. The
    panel never auto-saves - user always clicks Save.
  - Frontend panel: web/src/features/settings/components/QuietHoursPanel.tsx
    Renders the QuietHoursWindow form + list. Save POSTs to canonical
    /api/v1/notifications/quiet-hours via useQuietHoursWindows hook.
  - Backend canonical CRUD route: POST/PUT/DELETE /api/v1/notifications/quiet-hours
    handler at internal/api/quiet_hours_handler.go. Validation rules
    in internal/database/quiet_hours_repo.go enforce HH:MM, weekday
    bitmask, IANA timezone, severity subset (info|warn|critical).
  - The save path on the panel is the SOLE write path. The Helix
    advisor never POSTs to the canonical CRUD route - it returns a
    typed proposal and the user clicks Apply to form -> Save.

New AI surface (only present when ai_mode != off AND
quiet-hours-suggestion toggle on):
  - Backend route: POST /api/v1/ai/settings/quiet-hours/draft
    handler at internal/api/ai_quiet_hours_suggestion_handler.go,
    guarded by ai.GuardedHandler('quiet-hours-suggestion'). Returns
    404 in off mode (proven by Go test
    TestQuietHoursSuggestionAIOffManualSettingsWork).
  - Strategy: internal/ai/strategies/quiet-hours-suggestion/strategy.go
    SystemPrompt pins propose-only contract, allowed tools whitelist
    {draft_quiet_hours_window, validate_quiet_hours_window},
    PolicyAlertBuilder redaction policy, 3 goldens.
  - Tools: internal/ai/tools/quiet_hours_suggestion.go - typed F4
    tools, scope binding. The validator mirrors the canonical
    QuietHoursWindow rules used by the CRUD handler verbatim.
  - SPA component: web/src/components/ai/AIQuietHoursSuggestion.tsx
    AIFeatureCard + useAiStream + tool_result capture +
    onApplyDraft handoff. withAiFeature gate -> absent in off mode.
  - QuietHoursPage mounts AIQuietHoursSuggestion above
    QuietHoursPanel; shared seedDraft state forwards typed scalars
    via QuietHoursPanel's seedDraft prop (consumed once via
    ref-guarded useEffect, then cleared via onSeedConsumed).

Registry coverage (must be exhaustive for CoverageOK + aivet):
  - Backend:   POST /api/v1/ai/settings/quiet-hours/draft
  - Frontend:  /settings/notifications
  - UITestIDs: ai-feature-quiet-hours-suggestion-root
  - JobNames:  []   (no background jobs; conscious empty)
  - PushKinds: []   (no push notifications; conscious empty)

=== REASONING ===
Slice 0053 implements a P2 LLM advisor that proposes ONE quiet-hours
window from notification history WITHOUT mutating the canonical
QuietHoursWindow store. Structural pattern follows slice 0052
(pii-redaction-shared-exports) for the registry/handler/SPA scaffold,
plus slice 0034 (alert-tuning-suggestions) for the typed-proposal
render contract (tool_result -> Apply to form -> seed baseline form).

ADR-015 alignment:
  - I3 (baseline intact): QuietHoursPanel CRUD path is unchanged.
    The Helix advisor only adds an opt-in section above the panel.
    The canonical Save button on the panel remains the SOLE write
    path. Apply to form just pre-fills local form state.
  - I5 (hidden UI):  withAiFeature returns null when off ->
    component is absent from the DOM (proven by 3-case Vitest off
    contract).
  - I6 (404 routes): ai.GuardedHandler returns 404 when ai_mode='off'
    or per-feature toggle off (proven by Go test
    TestQuietHoursSuggestionAIOffManualSettingsWork).
  - I7 (per-feature): Both ai_mode=off AND toggle=false hide the
    surface (per-feature opt-in respected).
  - I8 (propose-only contract): Tools are read-only or pure
    validators; no SQL writes from feature code; mutations only
    flow through the canonical CRUD handler when the user clicks
    Save on QuietHoursPanel after applying the draft.
  - I10 (type system): QuietHoursDraftProposal narrows to fields
    consumed by the baseline form so the panel cannot be poisoned
    with extra fields the user did not consent to changing.

Decorator chain order (locked by methodology): redaction, rate
limit, cost cap, audit, trace - applied via the foundation P5
chain, not re-implemented per-strategy.

Eval mock-provider gotcha (carried from slice 0052): YAML literal
block scalars (|) preserve newlines, breaking strings.Contains
substring match on phrases that wrap across YAML lines. Canned
replies for this slice keep all load-bearing pin substrings on a
single physical line.

